(669120, 69738, 13035, '<td valign="top">What a great shot. I hope it does well.  I like the blur of the jumprope, the expression the childs face, the crop (and I don''t usually like tall skinny crops), the light, and the slin tones.  Nice post.  8</td>', 'What a great shot. I hope it does well.  I like the blur of the jumprope, the expression the childs face, the crop (and I don''t usually like tall skinny crops), the light, and the slin tones.  Nice post.  8', '2004-04-14 23:58:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(669124, 69189, 8125, '<td valign="top">Either this is really noisy from a low light situation, or it was out of focus and you tried to correct it by oversharpening.  I think the use of b/w is good and I like how you showed the strength needed to blow that horn.</td>', 'Either this is really noisy from a low light situation, or it was out of focus and you tried to correct it by oversharpening.  I think the use of b/w is good and I like how you showed the strength needed to blow that horn.', '2004-04-15 00:01:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(669127, 70123, 8125, '<td valign="top">Wow... this is a really interesting composition.  I like it.  I really like the use of b/w as well.  You do have some hot spots on the water that you might try to fix by dodge/burn on your final image.<br/> <br/>Edit: From my laptop those hot spots looked worse.  On my CRT - it''s not a problem.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-04-21 08:38:45.</i></td>', 'Wow... this is a really interesting composition.  I like it.  I really like the use of b/w as well.  You do have some hot spots on the water that you might try to fix by dodge/burn on your final image. Edit: From my laptop those hot spots looked worse.  On my CRT - it''s not a problem.', '2004-04-15 00:03:25.000000', '2004-04-21 09:38:45.000000', 1),
