(679362, 69781, 13077, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments. <br/>No, there wasn''t a fence between me and the dog, but he was running past me.<br/>The dog was near the left side of the frame, so I couldn''t have centered it.<br/>I couldn''t really do much about the background, I was just lucky to have my camera ready when he came charging past.<br/>The subject is dark, because the sky was really bright (cloudy, and approaching sunset), and that''s what the camera focused on for light metering.</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments. No, there wasn''t a fence between me and the dog, but he was running past me.The dog was near the left side of the frame, so I couldn''t have centered it.I couldn''t really do much about the background, I was just lucky to have my camera ready when he came charging past.The subject is dark, because the sky was really bright (cloudy, and approaching sunset), and that''s what the camera focused on for light metering.', '2004-04-21 12:05:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(679437, 69194, 17536, '<td valign="top">I''ve had some people ask how this was done, what was the trick? There is no trick. The glass really is balancing on plying cards. The possible trick is that the cards are taped together and there is a fourth card taped to the back of the ace for added stability. Other than that, it''s a straightforward shot.</td>', 'I''ve had some people ask how this was done, what was the trick? There is no trick. The glass really is balancing on plying cards. The possible trick is that the cards are taped together and there is a fourth card taped to the back of the ace for added stability. Other than that, it''s a straightforward shot.', '2004-04-21 12:30:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(679438, 70123, 19977, '<td valign="top">Congretulations. We hope you keep learning. What can we expect then in future challenges? Very well done.</td>', 'Congretulations. We hope you keep learning. What can we expect then in future challenges? Very well done.', '2004-04-21 12:31:07.000000', NULL, 0),
